# Supabase Migration Rules

Starting Oct 30, 2026, Supabase no longer auto-grants Data API access to new tables in `public`. Every new `create table public.<x>` must include explicit GRANTs and RLS, otherwise `supabase-js` / PostgREST / GraphQL will return `42501`.

## Required pattern for every new public table

```sql
create table public.your_table (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()
  -- ...
);

grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to authenticated;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to service_role;
-- Only if anonymous (logged-out) read is required:
-- grant select on public.your_table to anon;

alter table public.your_table enable row level security;

create policy "..." on public.your_table for select to authenticated using (...);
-- + insert/update/delete policies as needed
```

## Rules

- Never create a `public` table without RLS enabled.
- Never create a `public` table without at least `authenticated` + `service_role` grants — even if RLS is on, missing grants block PostgREST entirely.
- Only grant to `anon` when the table is intentionally readable by logged-out users.
- For server-only tables (accessed solely from edge functions via service role), still add `service_role` grant and skip `authenticated`/`anon`.
- Never edit historical migrations — add a new migration for grant/policy changes.
